<title>USA: TransTexas sees $600 mln pre-tax gain in Q2.</title>
<headline>TransTexas sees $600 mln pre-tax gain in Q2.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransTexas Gas Corp said Thursday it will record more than a $600 million gain in its second quarter ended July 31 as a result of the sale of its Lobo Trend unit.</p>
<p>The company gave no specific earnings estimates. Company officials were not immediately available to comment further.</p>
<p>The company said Thursday it lost $0.20 per share in its first quarter, compared with a profit of $0.04 per share in the same year-earlier period.</p>
</text>
